
 <!-- 1. Student Registration Form (Checking) -->

<!-- Description -->
This program is a student registration form. It allows users to enter student name, age, gender, and faculty. It validates the information and displays the results in a ListBox.

 <!-- Concepts Used -->

1. Variables: Used to store student information such as name, age, gender, and faculty.
2. String: Used to store text.
3. Integer (int): Used to store whole numbers.
4. TryParse(): Checks and converts the age into a number.
5. If Statement:Checks conditions.
6. Else If: Checks another condition when the first condition is false.
7. Else: Executes when the condition is false.
8. Nested If:An if statement inside another if statement.
9. RadioButton: Used to select one gender.
10. CheckBox:Used to select one or more faculties.
11. Checked: Checks whether a RadioButton or CheckBox is selected.
12. ListBox:Displays student information.
13. MessageBox: Displays error messages.
14. Clear(): Clears the TextBox and ListBox.
15. Event Handling: Handles button clicks.

<!-- Validation Rules -->
- Age must be a number.
- Age must be greater than zero.
- The user must select one gender.
- The user must select at least one faculty.

---

 <!-- 2. File Handling (Course File) -->

 <!-- Description -->
This program creates a text file called `course.txt`, writes course names into the file, and reads the courses into a ListBox.

 <!-- Concepts Used -->

1. File Handling: Used to create, write, and read files.
2. StreamWriter: Used to write data into a file.
3. StreamReader: Used to read data from a file.
4. File.CreateText(): Creates a new text file.
5. File.OpenText():Opens a text file for reading.
6. WriteLine(): Writes data line by line.
7. ReadLine(): Reads one line at a time.
8. While Loop: Repeats reading until the end of the file.
9. Null: Checks whether there is no more data to read.
10. ListBox:Displays the course names.
11. Try and Catch: Handles errors in the program.
12. Exception:Stores error information.
13. MessageBox: Displays error messages.
14. Close():Closes the file after reading or writing.

 <!-- Courses Added -->
- Intro to Nursing
- Arabic
- Calculus I
- Music Appreciation

 <!-- Program Functions -->
- Create a course file.
- Write course names into the file.
- Read course names from the file.
- Display courses in a ListBox.

---

 <!-- Conclusion -->

These two assignments demonstrate important C# concepts, including variables, data validation, conditional statements, loops, event handling, and file handling. They help me understand how to create Windows Forms applications and manage data using C#.